speechtext:
Yes, there have been consultations through various means:
(a)	the Public Service 2000 consultative committee includes four former senior officials-two former secretaries to the cabinet from the Ontario and Quebec governments, two former senior federal officials- Gaetan Lussier and Jaffray Wilkins;
(b)	the Public Service Commission undertook a survey of senior public servants who had recently left the Public Service;
(c)	many less formal consultations with former public servants, most of whom incorporated their views into articles or speeches, such as Gordon Osbaldeston, former secretary to the cabinet, Jack Manion, former associate secretary to the cabinet and John Carson, former chairman, Public Service Commission.
